# Parallax sketch tileset (pass 4, lace). One char = one pixel; `.` is transparent.
# A piece is <wtiles> x <htiles> tiles; its rows are wtiles*tile characters wide.
# Foreground (pixel defocus; author, 2026-11-19): every piece uses one neutral near-black palette (a body, b toward a
# standing piece's foot, c bark and midribs), a solid 1 px moon rim d on the edges facing the moon (up and right) with e
# behind it, dithered (e, f) only where it fades toward the foot of a standing piece; hanging pieces keep the full rim. The
# unlit edge is a soft alpha step g; outside it the fringe g, h and a dithered i, and a lit fringe j beside the rim. No
# Gaussian. Placed as tile objects (tools/parallax_mock.py). Rule B (author, 2026-11-19): the foreground may cover the walk
# edge and the hero, even fully, but never a trap, its cue, an enemy, a pickup or a used mechanism part, never the hero above
# the waist at the room start and exit, and never hides the hero for more than 0.5 s of walking. Pieces are open (lace):
# separate stems, fronds, blades and leaves with gaps the play shows through, thinnest where they cross the hero's band.
tile 16
color a 030303
color b 010101
color c 0e0d11
color d 7d8db0
color e 3c4865
color f 1d2335
color g 030303c0
color h 03030380
color i 03030348
color j 3c486578
# The near pieces (near-*, D113) add three body tones between a and the rim e: k, l and m, the steps from the body to the moonlit
# side of a leaf. Value steps in a near piece: a body, k, l, m, then the rim e and the lit fringe j.
color k 0d0e14
color l 1a1e2c
color m 2a3248

piece tuft 7 4
